course: dictionary
lesson: 1783
title: Clingy: wanting to be close
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Clingy describes someone, or something, that holds on tight and does not want to let go. Look at the words around it for clues. In «a clingy toddler», the word toddler tells you it is a little child, and clingy shows the child wants a grown-up close by at all times.
explain: Clingy can also describe clothes and material. «A clingy T-shirt» sticks closely to your body, and «clingy plastic wrap» sticks to a bowl or a plate. The clue is in what the thing touches: it clings to it.
explain: Pets and friends can be clingy too. A «clingy friend» may always want to sit next to you, and a «clingy kitten» may follow you from room to room. In family talk, clingy is sometimes used as a bit of teasing, but it still means wanting to be close.
fact: Clingy means always wanting to be close to someone and not wanting to be left alone.
fact: «A clingy toddler» needs a grown-up close by, and may cry when left.
fact: Clingy can also describe clothes or material that sticks closely to the body or to things.
fact: «A clingy T-shirt» fits close to your body, and «clingy plastic wrap» sticks to a dish.
fact: In family talk, clingy can be used as a bit of gentle teasing.
exercise: «The clingy toddler cried every time her mum left the room.» What does clingy mean here? | *Always wanting to be close and not wanting to be left alone | Very tall for her age | Happy to play alone in a quiet room | Quick to run and hide
exercise: Which phrase describes clothes or material? | a clingy friend who follows you everywhere | *a clingy T-shirt that sticks to your body | a clingy toddler who needs a grown-up
exercise: Nadia says clingy is just a fancy word for naughty. Why is she wrong? | Clingy means loud and rude to other people | Clingy means being very quick at running | *Clingy means wanting to be close and not wanting to be left alone | Clingy means being happy on your own
test: «The clingy kitten followed me everywhere and would not let me go.» What does clingy mean here? | Hiding under the bed | Sticking to the floor like glue | Wanting to be far away from everyone | *Wanting to be close and not wanting to be left alone
test: Which sentence uses clingy about a person? | *Our baby brother is so clingy that he cries when Dad goes to work. | The clear sky was clingy and blue. | The bus was clingy and drove very fast.
exam: Mum says, «Don't be so clingy», to her son. What does she mean? | He is wearing a T-shirt that is too big | *He always wants to be close to her and does not want to be left alone | He is hiding his toys under the bed | He is sitting very still and quiet
